  "body": "From the review of PR #1576 (pullrequestreview-5900373722). After #1576, a closed shell whose mesh has real gaps (e.g. two user parts with up to 2-4 mm of wall missing on a B-spline face) is refused at import. Correct under the Prime Directive, but the part cannot even be loaded for viewing or setup.\n\nA cheap 'incomplete but loadable' path exists: `schema::ReducedFidelity` with `model_fidelity::UNKNOWN_MM` already lets a model load while every operation is refused by name at the post and the program sim gives no verdict. Reusing it needs a stored cause (so the refusal names the hole, not a coarse chord), saved and loaded with the project.\n\nDone means: such a shell loads, is shown as incomplete with the hole named, and every operation on it is refused by name at the post; pinned. The real fix stays #1602 (mesh those faces).",
